  "historical_output_text": " I still recall a brisk spring day as if the wind were a whisper on paper instead of my own memory, the way the breeze tango’d against trees’ bare branches with barely-a-spring chill, like a reminder. The sky was that kind-of-weather gray – neither quite the light that’s still dark in winter’s hold yet too pale and watereasy to count it spring, but the color of old paper or cheap copy machines, that you see more in photos or on screen these old-school days, than with actual daylight outside the screen you watch.\n\nI strolls down familiar roads I've known from early morning school days and back when we played at each corner of this city like its secret, a playground for all, but the only one that mattered. Each turn, street and corner felt just a touch more real now than I’d",
